      "message": "Thank you for contributing, but without a specific test scenario or bug, I am very hesitant to accept a patch to Ganesh\u0027s clipping code at this point. Additionally, its pixel snapping for both inner and outer bounds is intentionally conservative to deal with the unknown behavior of a GPU rasterizing non-AA geometry/clips having to combine with anti-aliased geometry/clips.\n\nGanesh is effectively deprecated at this point and Graphite has a more robust contains() implementation that is based on the underlying floating point geometry.",
